//  PETPORTS -- CROSSHAIR: PLAIN
//
//  A MARKER, NOT A WEAPON. It exists so a player can see that a drop is spoken
//  for -- which matters most when a unit vent-routes, disappears, and surfaces
//  somewhere else. Without it that reads as the network ignoring the item.
//
//  STATIONARY AND HARMLESS, and every field below is load-bearing for one of
//  those two:
//
//    speed 0 + physics "laser"   never moves, never falls. Vanilla's energyzone
//                                is the same recipe, and it sits where it is
//                                cast until it times out.
//    damageTeamType "ghostly"    interacts with no entity at all. Belt and
//                                braces alongside power 0 and NoDamage: a
//                                marker that can be hit, blocked or reflected
//                                by anything is a bug waiting to happen on a
//                                populated server.
//    onlyHitTerrain false        it should not interact with terrain either.
//    orientationLocked           the sprite must not rotate to a flight vector
//                                it does not have.
//    fullbright                  legible in an unlit cave, which is exactly
//                                where a player most wants to know a drop was
//                                seen.
//    renderLayer                 ForegroundEntity+1. Above the terrain
//                                foreground, so a marker on a drop in a trench
//                                or behind a platform stays visible -- which is
//                                exactly where a player most wants to know an
//                                item was seen. Player+1 drew over the player;
//                                ItemDrop+1 sat behind foreground tiles.
//
//                                THE LAYER NAME IS LOOKED UP IN A MAP AND AN
//                                UNKNOWN ONE IS FATAL TO THE ASSET, not merely
//                                ignored:
//
//                                  Could not read projectile '...', error:
//                                  (MapException) Key 'Foreground' not found
//                                  in Map::get()
//
//                                So the projectile does not load at all and
//                                every spawn of it fails. "Foreground" is not
//                                in the vocabulary; "ForegroundEntity" is.
//
//  TIME TO LIVE IS A SAFETY NET, NOT THE LIFECYCLE, and it is LONG on purpose.
//
//  The port kills these by message the moment a state changes, and a new marker
//  culls any predecessor on the same item, so they normally die on command. The
//  TTL only matters when neither happens -- a port that unloads or crashes
//  mid-task -- because a stationary projectile with no expiry would be a
//  permanent artefact in someone's save.
//
//  IT WAS 3 SECONDS, WHICH MADE IT THE LIFECYCLE BY ACCIDENT. The port had to
//  respawn every marker every two seconds just to outrun it, so a marker
//  sitting quietly on an untouched drop was destroyed and rebuilt roughly
//  thirty times a minute, each rebuild leaving a predecessor for the cull to
//  clean up. Thirty seconds makes renewal rare and leaves an orphan visible for
//  at most half a minute -- and only until the next marker on that item evicts
//  it anyway.
//
//  WHITE SPRITE, BLACK OUTLINE, RECOLOURED PER SPAWN. The caller passes
//  processing "?multiply=RRGGBBAA": white takes the colour, black stays black.
//  Same trick the watering droplet uses to arrive blue.

{
	"projectileName" : "petports_crosshair",
	"image" : "petports_crosshair.png",

	"physics" : "laser",
	"speed" : 0,
	"timeToLive" : 30.0,

	"animationCycle" : 1.0,
	"frameNumber" : 1,

	"orientationLocked" : true,
	"fullbright" : true,
	"renderLayer" : "ForegroundEntity+1",

	"onlyHitTerrain" : false,
	"piercing" : true,
	"bounces" : -1,

	"power" : 0.0,
	"damageType" : "NoDamage",
	"damageKind" : "default",
	"damageTeamType" : "ghostly",

	"actionOnReap" : [ ],
	"periodicActions" : [ ],
	"emitters" : [ ],
	"pointLight" : false,

	"scripts" : [ "/projectiles/lofty_petports/petports_crosshair/petports_crosshair.lua" ]
}
